# Nothing is named off `b`: it is only read under an index. It is asked in front so that the length in its cell may stand there and not in every turn: what that needs is that no other thread grows its memory.
# It was asked for its names too, which an heir (class Samples extends Int32Array) or a view whose prototype was changed never has: the whole loop took the closed copy: 1,000 elements 179,166 instructions,
# 37,110 in front of that question, plain Bun 11,520. Its storage alone is asked: 12,174. `a`, whose `length` is named, is asked for both as before: an heir with a length of its own goes by that.
# f4 = go
# RUN: walk f4:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = IsPristine {{*}} builtinClass=TypedArray aspects=[Storage, Names]
# CHECK: = IsPristine {{*}} builtinClass=TypedArray aspects=[Storage]
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
